you> assistant> The reason metal spoons feel colder than wooden spoons is not because of their temperature, but because of how quickly they move heat away from your skin.

This phenomenon is explained by a concept in physics called **thermal conductivity**.

### 1. Thermal Conductivity
Every object has a specific ability to conduct heat. 
*   **Metals are thermal conductors:** They have high thermal conductivity. This means they are very efficient at moving heat from one place to another.
*   **Wood is a thermal insulator:** It has low thermal conductivity. It resists the flow of heat.

### 2. What your skin actually senses
When you touch an object, your nerves do not actually measure the object's absolute temperature. Instead, they measure the **rate at which heat is leaving your skin.**

